# Every checkout gets LF, on every platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic. depmesh records the byte size of each scanned file in
# the analysis model, and the demo page embeds that model. With the default
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows, a CRLF checkout makes every source file two
# bytes per line larger, so the model - and therefore the committed demo - differs
# between platforms even though the code is identical. The Windows CI leg caught
# exactly this: the same commit produced a demo that no longer matched itself.
#
# Pinning LF makes the byte counts, and thus the generated artifacts, identical
# everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts must never be converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
